>> serving: 6

Heat the air fryer on ''160C'' for ~{2 mins}. 

Mix the melted @butter{60%g}, @yogurt{75%g}, @egg{1} and @milk{2%tbsp} in a #large bowl{}

Fold in the @cast sugar{100g}, @flour{150%g}, @baking powder{8%g} and @bicarbonate of soda{1/4%tsp} and combine well.

Fold in the @blueberries, chocolate chips or dried fruit{75%g}, if using. Spoon the mixture into silicone cases or an air fryer muffin tin filled with paper cases to three-quarters full. You should be able to make ''6'' muffins, but you may have to bake them in batches.

Place the cases or tin in the air fryer basket and cook for ~{15 mins} until the muffins are golden brown and a skewer inserted into the centre comes out clean.